I(78,[78],'self-flagged step',[24,26],'619–632;706–716','conv. simple des coefficients','The (m,X)-adic topology on A[[X]] is the product coefficientwise m-adic topology: membership in (m,X)^p imposes a_j∈m^(p−j) for j<p.','This explains the marginal request; the finite coefficient conditions suffice without assuming A separated.','agrees','The manuscript’s coefficient criterion and summation proof give exactly the required topology comparison.')
I(79,[79],'unproved claim',[26],'720–735','E complet; F séparé; G(u) surjectif','For exhaustive decreasing filtrations, a filtered map from complete E to separated F with surjective graded map is strict surjective.','The conclusion is reconstructed because the retained sheet stops after hypotheses; successive error correction proves it.','agrees','The omitted conclusion/proof is not silently inserted in the transcription; later pages use the same method.')
I(80,[80],'unpursued implication',[41],'1070–1080','E/E_n→Ê/Ê_n ... bijectifs','Separated completion preserves every filtration quotient and hence the associated graded ring/module; multiplication and module action extend continuously.','Quotients are discrete, not necessarily finite; the nearby unhatted A in the topology sentence is flagged.','agrees','This is not a claim that E=Ê or that completion is faithful on an unrestricted category.')
I(81,[81],'reading question',[43],'1102–1111','homomorphismes topologiques','Completion preserves a strict exact sequence of metrizable abelian topological groups; continuity alone is insufficient.','Strictness means quotient topology equals the image’s induced topology. Q_discrete→Q_usual→0 refutes a continuity-only reading.','agrees','The older terminology is material. K62-01 scan55 lines76–92 uses the same term after verifying the quotient/induced equality.')
I(82,[82],'idea of the earlier run',[43],'1111','le composé ... est un homomorphisme','Strict maps are not closed under arbitrary composition: Z→R, n↦nα, and R→R/Z are strict for irrational α, while their composite has dense nondiscrete image.','The exact-sequence proof can instead use its particular quotient/closed-embedding factorization.','agrees','This diagnoses a general proof shortcut rather than refuting the properly formulated strict-completion lemma.')
