I(84,[84],'idea of the earlier run',[47,45],'1191;1134','U(g) ... noethérien','For noetherian K, finite generation of g as a K-module ensures U(g) is left/right noetherian. Without it, an infinite-dimensional abelian g gives k[x₁,x₂,...].','A standing finiteness convention may exist outside these sheets; the supplied assertion has none.','agrees','The ascending variable ideals refute the unrestricted statement; the filtered proof only needs a finite polynomial surjection onto gr U.')
