I(86,[86],'unpursued implication',[47,49],'1187–1189;1215–1223','G(E) ... de type fini ... noethérien','For separated filtered E over complete filtered A with the standard exhaustive bounded-below conventions, finite/noetherian gr E implies finite/noetherian E. In particular gr A noetherian implies A noetherian.','Successive lifts prove finite generation; induced filtrations on submodules prove noetherianity. The missing sum in line1215 is flagged.','agrees','The source puts completeness on A and separatedness on E, and these hypotheses cannot be suppressed.')
I(87,[87],'unpursued implication',[49],'1225–1227','A complet et E séparé','If A is m-adically complete and E m-adically separated, finitely many lifts generating E/mE generate E; E is not assumed finite.','Coefficient lifting proves the claim. E=k((t)) over k[[t]] shows separatedness is essential.','agrees','The page states finite generation as conclusion, so ordinary finite-module Nakayama is not a sufficient restatement.')
