I(92,[92],'self-flagged step',[37],'937–945','dégager ... les lemmes sur les groupes ordonnés','If G⊂G′ are ordered abelian groups with G′/G torsion, intersection induces a bijection of convex subgroups and preserves rank.','The clean injectivity proof uses a positive multiple in G and convexity; the assertion that a quotient embeds is not used.','agrees','The question concerns extracting the lemma, while the rank argument is substantially given.')
I(93,[93],'unpursued implication',[37,35],'947–949;896–898','L ... extension finie de K','A nontrivial discrete rank-one valuation remains discrete under a finite field extension, and conversely. Algebraic extensions preserve rank but can have value group Q and fail discreteness.','The tower of roots of a uniformizer supplies the infinite-extension contrast.','agrees','The finite-extension hypothesis is explicit, and the printed continuation completes the finitely generated rank-one argument.')
